From 303dcac9e995ed35562b378b39be65f08c32ee8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 16:35:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: st: omit unused pinctrl groups from stm32mp21 dtb
 files

stm32mp21-pinctrl.dtsi gathers all pinctrl groups from current and future
STM32MP21-based boards. Some groups may remain unused by any board,
resulting in wasted binary space.
Adding /omit-if-no-ref/ to the groups will remove unused groups from the
device tree blobs.

Use the following regex to update the file:
's/^\t[^:]\+: [^ ]\+ {$/\t\/omit-if-no-ref\/\n&/'

Change-Id: I25a4f51cd47a90586b8ad977421774723b0fe92c
Signed-off-by: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/545337
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
